    "annotations": [
      {
        "id": "a1",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Tunnel-diode oscillator.** One 0-junction carries the tank voltage v. Its branches: the capacitor C (1-junction Jc with the current detector Ic), the inductor L (1-junction Jl, Il), the tunnel diode (a nonlinear R, i = -a v + b v^3 about its bias point) and the voltage detector Vm. C v' = -i_L + a v - b v^3 and L i_L' = v.",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 640,
        "w": 720,
        "h": 90
      },
      {
        "id": "a2",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Van der Pol scaling.** tau = w0 t with w0 = 1/sqrt(L C), x = v/A with A = sqrt(a/(3 b)): x'' - mu (1 - x^2) x' + x = 0 with mu = a sqrt(L/C). Xc and Yc are the circuit's x and x'; Ref integrates the textbook equation in the circuit's seconds.",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 760,
        "w": 720,
        "h": 80,
        "color": "blue"
      },
      {
        "id": "a3",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Energy.** Tank/E = C v^2/2 + L i_L^2/2; Split integrates the diode power: W_sup while it supplies (|v| < sqrt(a/b)), W_abs while it dissipates. Tank/E + Split/W stays constant; on the limit cycle Meter/dw1 = Meter/dw2 (supplied = dissipated per cycle).",
        "x": 860,
        "y": 840,
        "w": 700,
        "h": 90,
        "color": "green"
      }
    ]
  },
